> ERROR: Parameter "mem" is null.

@bruvzg This error suggests that it is running out of memory. The allocation that it is doing here is in the order of 10K and Jolt should use in the order of 10 MB (configurable in the settings). When I run the MRP of #105455, according to task manager my process uses about 55 MB of RAM and I'm unable to reproduce this issue. Note that I had to clean the `bin/obj/modules/jolt_physics` and `bin/obj/thirdparty/jolt_physics` folders because somehow scons didn't recompile after updating `Memory.h`. Maybe you have a mix between the old and the new code?

> Maybe ensuring that Jolt (well here the whole of Godot) is compiled with -msse2 -mfpmath=sse -mstackrealign would solve the issue?

@akien-mga `-mstackrealign` might be a good idea to add to ensure that the stack stays 16 byte aligned, although I have no evidence at this moment that we have stack alignment issues. `-mfpmath=sse` will probably improve performance for all of godot but I don't think it will help with this particular issue. For a large part Jolt already uses SSE2 as the intrinsics that it uses don't get converted to x87 fp instructions.
